Continual-ARC demos can vary radically in grid size, palette, and apparent motif. Do not conclude they are unrelated solely from those differences, and do not unify them based on superficial shared colors or density. For each pair, extract the exact input-output changes and describe the transformation in role-level terms (background, marker/seed, copied footprint, output color). Compare those abstractions across all pairs. A compelling candidate must reproduce every demo cell-for-cell, including cells left unchanged and explicit background-valued positions in any stamped footprint. If no common validated rule emerges, another demo is more valuable than a speculative submission when the remaining budget permits.

